### 1. TECHNICAL & ARCHITECTURAL RULES (STRICT)
- Deliver exactly 3 files: index.html, style.css, script.js.
- Tech Stack: Pure HTML5, CSS3, and Vanilla JavaScript. NO external libraries, frameworks, fonts, images, or CDNs. 
- Assets: Use CSS shapes, inline SVG, emojis, or canvas procedural drawing. Use the Web Audio API for zero-dependency retro sound effects (synthesized beeps/pops that fail silently if unsupported).
- Architecture: Write clean, modular, object-oriented or well-scoped functional JS. Use a single robust state machine and a single requestAnimationFrame game loop with delta-time clamping (preventing huge jumps on tab switch).
- Robustness: Wrap localStorage in try/catch. Auto-pause when the window/tab loses focus. Prevent double-start bugs and input spam.

### 2. UI/UX & VISUAL DESIGN DIRECTION
- Theme: Create a cohesive, premium indie-game aesthetic tailored to the game's theme (rich color palette using CSS variables, custom typography stack, subtle glassmorphism, layered atmospheric background, and smooth shadows).
- States: Stunning opening screen with clear instructions and a glowing CTA; responsive HUD (score, high score, timer/level, pause button); polished pause overlay; and a dramatic game-over/victory screen with a "New Best!" celebration badge and Replay button.
- Feedback (Juice): Every action must feel satisfying. Implement micro-interactions, floating score popups, button hover/active states, screen shake on failure, and particle bursts or glow effects on success.

### 3. RESPONSIVE & MOBILE-FIRST CONTROLS
- Fully responsive from 320px to 1920px with zero horizontal scroll.
- Support both desktop (keyboard/mouse) and mobile (touch controls + large 44px+ on-screen touch buttons if applicable).
- Set viewport meta tag with viewport-fit=cover and touch-action: none to prevent accidental mobile page scrolling during gameplay.

